<!-- wp:column {"width":"60%"} -->
<div class="wp-block-column" style="flex-basis:60%"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>WordPress is made of parts: the core software, a theme and a set of plugins. Each part gets updates, mostly to close security holes and stay compatible with the others.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leave the updates and the site slowly becomes easier to break into. Apply them carelessly and two parts can clash, which is how a site ends up showing a blank page on a Monday morning.</p>
